# Inbox

#
# Module
#
ModuleInboxName = Inbox
ModuleInboxDesc = Mail foundation: one mail read by its Message-ID, .eml and .msg files parsed
ModuleInboxDescLong = Inbox reads one mail in a mailbox declared in CRM Client Connector, from its Message-ID, always read only (the mail stays unread). It also reads the mails given as files (.eml, Outlook .msg) with their attachments. Other modules use it, for example to prefill a quote from a customer request.

#
# Permissions
#
InboxRightMessageRead = Read a mail from its Message-ID
Permission14193001 = Read a mail from its Message-ID

#
# Setup
#
InboxSetup = Inbox setup
InboxSetupHelp = A mail is read only when its complete Message-ID is given: no listing, no search by sender or subject. Every reading is recorded in the journal.
InboxMailboxes = Mailboxes
InboxNoCrmClientConnector = The CRM Client Connector module is not enabled: the mailboxes and their IMAP access are set there. Only the mails given as files can be read.
InboxMailboxesHelp = %s mailbox(es) declared in CRM Client Connector. IMAP access is set on the Anti-spam tab of each email account.
INBOX_CACHE_DAYS = Keep the mails read in the cache for
INBOX_CACHE_DAYSHelp = A mail read from a mailbox is kept on the server so that it is not read again on the mail server. Modules that use it attach it to their record anyway.
INBOX_LOG_DAYS = Keep the journal of the readings for
INBOX_LOG_DAYSHelp = Who read which mail, from which mailbox, found or not.
InboxCronPurge = Inbox: purge of the cache and of the journal
InboxCronPurgeComment = Removes the mails read longer ago than the retention of the cache, and the old lines of the journal

InboxCache = Cache of the mails read
InboxCacheHelp = %s mail(s) in the cache (%s). Emptying it is harmless: a mail is read again on the mail server when needed.
InboxClearCache = Empty the cache
InboxClearCacheConfirm = Remove every mail of the cache? They will be read again on the mail server when needed. The journal of the readings is kept.
InboxCacheCleared = %s mail(s) removed from the cache

